                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "37688325",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198042831386",
                            "num_reviews": 627,
                            "playtime_forever": 569,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 569,
                            "last_played": 1511025691
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h1]Short version: 74%[/h1]\nThanks to its working Steam achievements, actual (yet simple) story, more memorable and eventful levels, and faster paced gameplay, Rescue Team 7 is one of the high points of this time management series.\n\n[h1]Long version:[/h1]\nSince this is the seventh entry in a series of time management games where the core gameplay has not changed since its creation, most players probably know the drill by now: in Rescue Team 7, we use rescue workers, doctors, firemen, policemen, dogs, and vehicles to collect resources, fix buildings, and save civilians.\n\nDespite looking like a copy-paste job of Rescue Team 6, this game hides quite a few surprises, chiefly in level design. Thanks to careful object placement, all stages feel a lot faster and busier, so gameplay is tighter and more fun—but it also requires more attention from the player, especially to meet some of the time requirements.\nThe puzzle levels also received a large overhaul: they now feature cavern exploration, where the goals require less guesswork and more focus on proper resource management.\n\nFor the first time since the third game, we also have an actual story. It is just a very simple romance between two workers, but its presence alone is enough to consider Rescue Team 7 a fun and memorable time management game, one of the best in its series.",
